"suggestion":"1. Implement the 'pulsing ring' visual state for nodes that are ready to be learned (i.e., have all prerequisites met and the user has available points). This is critical for aligning the visual design with the explicit UI instructions. 2. Add a subtle visual cue to the 'Save Build' button (e.g., a checkmark or 'Saved' state) to clarify its function and relationship to the current build. 3. Consider adding a small legend or tooltip system to the skill tree that explains the different node states (Locked, Available, Unlocked, Maxed) to reinforce the intended progression experience."
}

clarity_hierarchy.raw_response:
